  "notes": "Both images show the same RP2040-Tiny style artwork (product name not printed on the board in view); transcribed from each image separately. No USB connector is visible (only an FPC connector at the top), so the top/left rule is used. Silkscreen numbers beside the pads are GPIO numbers, kept as functions. The \"User mode selection pads\" (GP24/GND, GP25/GND) are solder-jumper selection pads and the WS2812 LED pin table is not a wiring point; both are skipped. Legend categories omitted."
